---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-time-picker</code> shows a column each for hours and minutes, and AM/PM on a 12-hour
  clock. It is the picker inside <code>wc-time-field</code>; for a form input, use
  <code>wc-time-field</code>.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-time-picker id='time-picker-demo' value='09:30'></wc-time-picker>
  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelector('#time-picker-demo').addEventListener('input', function (event) {
      myConsole.log('input :: ' + event.detail.value);
    });
    document.querySelector('#time-picker-demo').addEventListener('change', function (event) {
      myConsole.warn('change :: ' + event.detail.value);
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>
  The value is a 24-hour ISO time (<code>09:30</code>) whatever the display. Picking an hour fires
  <code>input</code>; picking in the last column, or pressing Enter, fires <code>change</code>.
</p>
